e every other page uses a section header, so the page reads as one continuous wall instead of parts.","value":"5 sections"},{"id":"filechip","on":true,"label":"Tag a document link with the format it opens","why":"43 links on this page open a file — 34 PDF, 9 Excel — and say nothing about it, while others in the same list carry a tag because their author typed one. The format is read from the file name, so the list stops being half-labelled. No link text changes.","value":"43 links"},{"id":"itemdash","on":true,"label":"Drop the dash once the link is set apart","why":"38 of those items separate the link from its description with a dash. The link is now set in the display face at a larger size with a chevron after it, so the dash marks a boundary that is already unmistakable. Only the separator is removed — no word changes.","value":"38 separators"},{"id":"items","on":true,"label":"Separate a link from its description","why":"38 list items open with a link and then explain it, all at the same weight — so the thing you can click is no easier to find than the sentence about it. The link becomes the item and the explanation sits under it.","value":"38 items"},{"id":"descap","on":true,"label":"Start a description with a capital","why":"1 description begins with a small letter, because it used to run on from the link after a dash. The dash is gone and the link now sits above in its own face, so each description opens a line of its own. One character changes and only ever the first.","value":"1 description"},{"id":"toc","on":true,"label":"Add a contents list (5 sections)","why":"Built from the section headings already on the page. Below three sections a list is not a route."},{"id":"eyebrow","on":true,"label":"Eyebrow: \"Essential Programs and Services (EPS) Funding\"","why":"Taken from the parent page, /funding/gpa/eps."}],"mechanical":["empty paragraphs removed: 1","drupal entity attrs stripped: 156","paragraph inside a list item unwrapped: 1","redundant bold inside a head